Jumping spell costs 5 mana to move two or three squares, compared to 20 
(40 with the Amulet) mana to teleport across an entire level.  So the 
spell is not an effective travel method, though still useful tactically.

Haste self costs 15 mana for ~105 turns [1] of "very fast", or one mana 
per seven turns.  If you use all seven of those turns to move, that's an 
additional 2.33 squares traveled, which is nice.  Also, you can stack up 
[tens|hundreds of] thousands turns of very fast, so it won't cost you any 
mana during the crucial endgame.

Oh, because every thread should contain nerfing discussion (Hi, Jove!), 
I'll say this:  Infinite stacking of Haste Self spell should be nerfed.  
Cap it at 500 turns, or 300, or whatever.



